/tmp/arxiv2309.sa4Qo1/main.tex:808:In the last step, i.e. $i=N$, construct the matching $M_N$ from $\cP_{N-1}$ as before. Thus, $|M_N|\le 2\beta^3|V_N|$ by \eqref{eq:M3}. Moreover since $(\cV,\cC,M_{abs},C_{abs})$ belongs to $\cS(\alpha,\alpha',\beta,\delta,\epsilon,N,\mathbb{G})$, we have that $|C_N|\ge \delta^{-1} |V_N|$, $\mathbb{G}_{C_N}[V_N]$ is not $\alpha'$-extremal, and $G_i[V_N]$ has minimum degree at least $(1/2-\epsilon)|V_N|$ for each $i\in C_N$ (see \Cref{def:vortex,def:vortexabsorber}). We let $G_N$ be the graph on $V_N$ such that $e\in E(G_N)$ if and only if $|\{i\in C_N:e\in E(G_i)\}|\ge |V_N|$. Therefore, for every vertex $v\in V_N$, we have
