I found one implementation edge case worth fixing before paying for oracle runs: `escalate()` could advance to sizes where the claimed compact route exceeds the 300-operation cap. I’m constraining the one admissible post-hard escalation and making construction enforce the cap there; larger arbitrary instances still build for G7, but they are not offered as shippable rungs.
