codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s fixed-cycle rainbow-coloring step.

Files:

- [gen_2309_12607.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/gen_2309_12607.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates all pass. Highlights:

- Inverse-generated affine Hamilton-cycle transversal.
- Exact verification without reading the planted answer.
- Guessing: 0/200,000; search space `107!`.
- Four no-tool attacks: 0/8 each.
- Honest Track B reference: Hopcroft–Karp, `O(E√V)`, 2,443 edge scans versus 266 modular operations for the compact route.
- Answer: 319 characters, 107 atoms.
- Canonical-key invariance: 80/80; unrelated distinctness: 20/20.

The paper was audited from its current full text: Sections 4–5 license the auxiliary matching interpretation. See the [arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.12607).

One external blocker remains: every bare, hinted, and placebo oracle request returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` before inference. The transcripts record errors—not model failures—so no hardness verdict has been claimed. Restore OpenRouter quota, then rerun the three harness commands documented in the README.
