codex
Implemented the verified Track B generator based on the paper’s fixed-cycle rainbow-coloring step.

Deliverables:

- [gen_2309_12607.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/gen_2309_12607.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four in-context attacks: 0/8 each.
- Hopcroft–Karp reference algorithm: 8/8, 2,443 edge scans.
- Answer: 319 characters, 107 atoms.
- Compact route: 266 exact operations.
- Canonicalization: 100/100 invariance checks and 20/20 distinct instances.

The family is honestly classified as a `paper_licensed` reduction, not full native-domain coverage: Section 5, Lemma 5.1 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.12607) identifies fixed-edge rainbow colorings with perfect matchings.

The required external hardness verdict remains incomplete. The refreshed bare run recorded one genuine oracle failure, after which OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every redraw. The G9 arms were similarly blocked. The script-owned evidence was retained without fabrication; once quota is restored, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2309.12607
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2309_12607.py
```
